// wql_graph_root_id_cross_document — ⚠ THIS FILE RECORDS AN OPEN DEFECT. IT IS
// A TRIPWIRE, NOT A RULING. EVERY ASSERTION BELOW ENCODES BEHAVIOUR THAT IS
// WRONG AND MEASURED, SO THAT THE DECISION TO CHANGE IT HAS A REPRO AND SO THAT
// CHANGING IT CANNOT HAPPEN SILENTLY.
//
// THE DEFECT. A node id in the graph vocabulary is supposed to identify a node.
// Container nodes get their Writ handle; scalar leaves get the synthetic
// FNV(parent handle, edge ordinal), which is unique because the parent handle
// is. The VIRTUAL ROOT EDGE has no parent node, so it passes the reserved
// parent word 0 and ordinal 0 — and therefore EVERY null-rooted or
// scalar-rooted document, on every binding time, gets the SAME root child id:
//
//     FNV-1a(0, 0) = 590684067820433389
//
// It is the only id in the whole vocabulary that does not depend on the
// document. Two unrelated documents that happen to have non-container roots are
// indistinguishable by `child`, so a join on `child` across two sources matches
// rows that name different nodes of different documents. Below: two documents
// whose roots are the integers 7 and 99 — different values, different
// documents, unrelated in every way — join on `child` and produce ONE row. The
// answer a correct id space gives is ZERO.
//
// PRE-EXISTING ON BOTH SIDES, and not created by the a5ce4915 alignment: the
// static walker already folded FNV(0,0), and the dynamic walker's earlier
// hand-written literal `1i64` was equally document-independent. Aligning them
// made one wrong value out of two; it did not introduce the collision.
//
// REACHABILITY, measured rather than assumed. The `**` reach relation and the
// gpath steps in logos.std.wql.lower join on `child` at four places, and ALL
// FOUR ARE SINGLE-SOURCE (`gp_reach_rel` builds `__reach_<src>` from one `src`,
// and the gpath step carries `src_name = src` on both sides), so no collision
// can arise there. Within one document none can arise either — every non-root
// leaf id is salted by a real parent handle, and handle 0 is reserved. The
// reachable surface is exactly a USER-WRITTEN cross-source join on `child`,
// which is the shape this file writes, and which the corpus already exercises
// in its non-colliding form (wql_writ_graph_e2e's `both_engines`, and
// query_gpath_e2e's two-tree `bind_source_tree` join).
//
// WHY THE FIX IS NOT IN THIS COMMIT. Both options the arc was handed turn out
// not to hold, and the third one is a RULING:
//
//   (a) mix a document handle into the root id — NOT SYMMETRICALLY
//       IMPLEMENTABLE. The static side has a document (`&Writ`); the dynamic
//       side has none, because `QEnv::bind_source_tree` stores `root.raw()` and
//       for a non-container root that word IS the value — two documents rooted
//       at 7 bind byte-identically. Making it coherent means a new document
//       identity in the public bind API.
//   (b) declare root ids document-scoped and refuse a cross-document join on
//       `child` — ENFORCEABLE ONLY AT THE DIRECT SITE. A rel column launders
//       the provenance (`rel r(a: i64) { from g e select e.child }`, then join
//       `g2` against `r.a`, which is a plain i64), and the rule would have to be
//       written twice because the static (`wql!` → codegen) and dynamic
//       (check.logos) checkers are separate. A gate that refuses the obvious
//       spelling and admits the laundered one is worse than a recorded gap: it
//       looks closed.
//   (c) salt the root id with the MATERIALIZATION's identity, so no id in the
//       vocabulary is reproducible across runs — symmetric, cheap, and it
//       retires the hand-derived literal that wql_graph_null_root_row pins and
//       the ruling in docs/spec/deem.md that fixes the value at every binding
//       time. That is a ruling, and rulings are not made inside a repair.
//
// WHEN THE RULING COMES, THIS FILE GOES RED. That is its job. The correct
// response is to REWRITE it against the new rule (the two documents' root ids
// DIFFER; the cross-document join answers 0 rows) — never to relax an
// assertion, and never to delete the file without replacing what it measures.
//
// Exit 0 iff the collision is still exactly as measured. Codes: 1x the static
// ids, 2x the static cross-document join, 3x the dynamic ids, 4x the dynamic
// cross-document join, 5x the within-document control, 9x setup.
package test;

use logos.lang.writ.container;
use logos.lang.writ.anyval;
use logos.std.wql.ir;
use logos.std.wql.wql;
use logos.std.wql.writ_graph;
use logos.mem.deem;
use logos.lang.result;
use logos.lang.str;
use logos.mem.collections.vec;

// The whole relation of one document — for a scalar root that is the root row
// alone, so `child` here IS the root id.
pub deem child_ids(g: &Writ) {
    from g e select e.child
}

// THE COLLISION, statically: two unrelated documents joined on a column that is
// supposed to identify a node. `select a.vi` proves which document the surviving
// row came from.
pub deem cross_child(a: &Writ, b: &Writ) {
    from a e1 join b e2 on e2.child == e1.child select e1.vi
}

// The CONTROL, same shape, a column with no identity claim: joining on `kind`
// is *supposed* to match across documents, so a spurious row there would mean
// the join machinery is matching everything and the leg above proves nothing.
pub deem cross_kind(a: &Writ, b: &Writ) {
    from a e1 join b e2 on e2.kind == e1.kind select e1.vi
}

// ── THE DYNAMIC HALF, WITHOUT THE QUERY INTERPRETER (2026-08-09) ────────────
// Legs 3 and 4 used to bind TWO tree sources into one `QEnv` and compile a
// cross-source join. `QEnv`/`Query` (stdlib/mem/deem/query.logos) and the
// walker's only caller (the QB_TSRC arm of `exec_rexpr`, exec.logos) are both
// on the P5 deletion list, so the OTHER BINDING TIME of this defect — the whole
// reason the file has legs 3 and 4 at all — would have vanished with them,
// leaving a tripwire that trips on one engine only.
//
// The cross-document join survives as a two-SLICE deem over two independent
// walks (`dyn_graph_edge_rows`, graphsrc.logos) — the same shape `cross_child`
// has over two `&Writ`s. The join is still a JOIN, not an `if`: the collision
// this file records is a property of the JOIN over the `child` column, so
// replacing it with a hand-written comparison would have retired the measurement
// while keeping the file.
pub deem child_ids_dyn(a: &[DynEdge]) {
    from a e select e.child
}
pub deem cross_child_dyn(a: &[DynEdge], b: &[DynEdge]) {
    from a e1 join b e2 on e2.child == e1.child select e1.vi
}

fn main() -> i32 {
    // hand-folded, see the header and wql_graph_null_root_row
    let synth: i64 = 590684067820433389i64;

    // two documents, unrelated: roots 7 and 99
    let da: Writ = writ_new(65536i64);
    let av: WAny = da.int(7i64);
    if !av.is_int() { return 90i32; }
    da.set_root(av);

    let db: Writ = writ_new(65536i64);
    let bv: WAny = db.int(99i64);
    if !bv.is_int() { return 91i32; }
    db.set_root(bv);

    // the two Writs are genuinely different documents
    if (&da as *const Writ) as i64 == (&db as *const Writ) as i64 { return 92i32; }

    // ── leg 1: the two root ids are EQUAL, and equal to the fold ────────────
    let ia: Vec<i64> = match child_ids(&da) { Result::Ok(v) => { v } Result::Err(_a) => { return 93i32; } };
    if ia.len() != 1i64 { return 93i32; }
    let ib: Vec<i64> = match child_ids(&db) { Result::Ok(v) => { v } Result::Err(_b) => { return 94i32; } };
    if ib.len() != 1i64 { return 94i32; }

    if ia.get(0i64) != synth { return 10i32; }
    if ib.get(0i64) != synth { return 11i32; }
    // ⚠ THE DEFECT, stated positively: two documents, one node id.
    if ia.get(0i64) != ib.get(0i64) { return 12i32; }

    // ── leg 2: a cross-document join on `child` answers 1 where 0 is right ──
    let x: Vec<i64> = match cross_child(&da, &db) { Result::Ok(v) => { v } Result::Err(_c) => { return 95i32; } };
    if x.len() != 1i64 { return 20i32; }        // ⚠ the correct answer is 0
    if x.get(0i64) != 7i64 { return 21i32; }    // and the row is doc A's root

    // ── leg 5: the control — the join machinery is not matching everything ──
    // `kind` carries no identity, so a match there is legitimate and tells the
    // reader that leg 2's single row is about `child` and not about the join.
    let k: Vec<i64> = match cross_kind(&da, &db) { Result::Ok(v) => { v } Result::Err(_d) => { return 96i32; } };
    if k.len() != 1i64 { return 50i32; }
    if k.get(0i64) != 7i64 { return 51i32; }

    // ── legs 3 and 4: the DYNAMIC engine, same two documents ───────────────
    // Same defect at the other binding time — the vocabulary is one vocabulary,
    // and so is its hole.
    let wa: Vec<DynEdge> = dyn_graph_edge_rows(av, &da);
    let wb: Vec<DynEdge> = dyn_graph_edge_rows(bv, &db);
    if wa.len() != 1i64 { return 97i32; }
    if wb.len() != 1i64 { return 98i32; }

    let ya: Vec<i64> = match child_ids_dyn(wa.as_slice()) { Result::Ok(v) => { v } Result::Err(_e) => { return 97i32; } };
    if ya.len() != 1i64 { return 97i32; }
    if ya.get(0i64) != synth { return 30i32; }

    let yb: Vec<i64> = match child_ids_dyn(wb.as_slice()) { Result::Ok(v) => { v } Result::Err(_f) => { return 98i32; } };
    if yb.len() != 1i64 { return 98i32; }
    if yb.get(0i64) != synth { return 31i32; }

    let y: Vec<i64> = match cross_child_dyn(wa.as_slice(), wb.as_slice()) { Result::Ok(v) => { v } Result::Err(_g) => { return 99i32; } };
    if y.len() != 1i64 { return 40i32; }        // ⚠ the correct answer is 0
    if y.get(0i64) != 7i64 { return 41i32; }

    return 0i32;
}
